From 650b7b0db39a37fea14d78970d3df72b113b5f73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:47:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 200/225] feat: debug view 13 - validator C, the reflection
 against the direct view in stops

Energy audit item 10 / section 5. The one test the picture cannot argue with:
for a ray hit that also happens to be visible to the camera, the reflected
shading of that point and the direct shading of the same point must agree.

e_svoTI_RT_Debug 13 projects the hit back through SVO_ViewProj, checks the depth
buffer says the camera really sees that surface (2 % of the hit distance, floor
5 cm) and not something in front of it, then paints
log2(luminance(reflected) / luminance(direct)) in stops:

  black = they agree                  red   = the reflection is N stops BRIGHTER
  blue  = not testable (off screen,   green = the reflection is N stops DARKER
          occluded, or a miss)

Both sides are read in EXPOSED units - `acc` is pre-divide and $HDRTargetPrev is
the pre-exposed HDR target - so the ratio is exposure-free by construction and
no exposure factor appears anywhere in the branch.

Two caveats, and they are why this lives only in a debug branch and why the two
resources are bound only for this view: $HDRTargetPrev is the PREVIOUS frame, so
the camera has moved and it is noisy in motion (judge it on a still frame), and
reading a pre-exposed buffer back into SVO maths is exactly what
e_svoTI_SSDepthTrace is forced to 0 for on the scene-referred path. The value
never leaves the debug branch. Both facts are in the cvar help string.

t4 (depth) and t12 ($HDRTargetPrev) are free on the ShadePass technique -
TiledShading.cfi's CausticsRT at t12 lives inside TILED_DEFERRED_SHADING_TECHNIQUE,
which this shader never compiles. SVO_ViewProj is uploaded here because ShadePass
deliberately does not call SetupCommonConstants.

